Steve,=0A=0AThe CIL policy is attached that is giving problems. =0A=0AI hav=
e this installed as the running policy so you may need to change the=0Arun-=
semanage script.=0A=0AIf you run run-semodule after creating the /var/lib/s=
elinux/<policy-name>/ =0Adirectory structure, it should install the policy =
okay.=0A=0AIf you then edit the x_select_paste.cil file you will find a com=
ment on line 111:=0A=0A; STEVE: Remove comment and then run run-semodule "E=
rror: Duplicate rule defined (line: 29)"=0A=0ASo remove the ';' on line 112=
 to read:=0A(typetransition x_select_paste_t unconfined_t x_drawable x_sele=
ct_paste_t)=0A=0Athe error should then appear. If you add/remove the ';' on=
 the other =0Atypetransition statements you will get different Dup line err=
ors.=0A=0ANote after removing ';' on line 112, run-cil will still build pol=
icy (remove a few more and it will also error).=0A=0AIt seems to be related=
 to the policy size as when I added the booleans after Eric's suggestion I =
found I had to remove more typetransition statements to get the policy to b=
uild.=0A=0AThanks for your help=0ARichard=0A=0ANote I build the same policy=
 as policy language modules using checkmodule with all the type_transition =
statements - with no errors.=0A=0A
